    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "38ad0d9a_350ca7c6",
        "filename": "common/keyboard_scan.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 272,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-09T20:29:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When c1 and c2 have at least one row is active in common,\n\n  1. no other rows in c2 are active -\u003e success\n  2. at least another row is active in common -\u003e ghost -\u003e reject\n  3. another row in c2 is active -\u003e new key press -\u003e reject\n\nIf I understand correctly, we can finish scanning only in case of #1. Then, the scan loop should be much tighter and more efficient (than this CL or the current loop).\n\n  r \u003d keyboard_raw_read_rows();\n  if (s \u0026 r \u0026\u0026 count_bits(r) \u003e 1)\n    return ERROR_MAYBE_GHOST;\n  state[c] \u003d r;\n  s |\u003d r;",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 261,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 272,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "da3eee1c07967445b7b481f4e859a88277c67a1b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
