      "writtenOn": "2019-12-09T20:58:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your second point is not always the case, in case one or more of the four coordinate points do not correspond to a actual keys, there is no ghosting even when c1 and c2 have two rows in common.  Whether this is the case is decided further down, using actual_key_mask, and the in has_ghosting.\n\nMy hope what that detecting ghosting could continue to be done using the same code, and that read_matrix would do this \"transitive closure\" to hide the fact that keys could have changed state during the scan.",
      "parentUuid": "38ad0d9a_350ca7c6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 261,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 272,
        "endChar": 42
      },
